--- a/vllm/v1/attention/backends/rocm_aiter_unified_attn.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/attention/backends/rocm_aiter_unified_attn.py
@@ -235,7 +235,7 @@
             max_seqlen_k=max_seqlen_k,
             softmax_scale=softmax_scale,
-            causal=True,
+            causal=(self.attn_type not in (AttentionType.ENCODER_ONLY, AttentionType.ENCODER)),
             alibi_slopes=self.alibi_slopes,
             window_size=self.sliding_window,
             block_table=block_table,

Fix for ROCm/aiter#1702: Make causal flag dynamic in rocm_aiter_unified_attn.py

The original code hardcodes causal=True, blocking bidirectional attention
needed by Gemma4's vision tokens. This patch makes it dynamic based on
the attention type:
- ENCODER_ONLY / ENCODER: causal=False (bidirectional)
- DECODER / ENCODER_DECODER: causal=True (autoregressive)

Apply inside container:
  docker exec gemma4-vllm python3 -c "
  path = '/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/attention/backends/rocm_aiter_unified_attn.py'
  with open(path) as f: c = f.read()
  c = c.replace('causal=True,', 'causal=(self.attn_type not in (AttentionType.ENCODER_ONLY, AttentionType.ENCODER)),', 1)
  with open(path, 'w') as f: f.write(c)
  "
